{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"content":"{\n  \"observed_vs_expected\": \"The experiment did not execute (rounds_executed=0, run_status='not_run'). Consequently, no metrics were observed. The expected observation of 'best_target_score increasing' and 'valid_candidates remaining positive' could not be verified because the optimization loop was never initiated. The compilation failed due to a schema ambiguity regarding layer order.\",\n  \"deviation_mechanism\": \"The failure is procedural, not physical. The research charter requires evaluating two distinct physical stack configurations (Air/SiO2/TiO2/Glass vs Air/TiO2/SiO2/Glass) within a single experimental run. However, the underlying TMM solver schema used for this route supports only one fixed layer sequence per execution. This creates a logical conflict where the optimizer cannot define a unique search space without knowing which material interfaces with air and which with glass. Therefore, no candidate thicknesses were generated or evaluated.\",\n  \"continue_recommended\": true,\n  \"continue_rationale\": \"Since zero rounds have been executed, there is no empirical evidence regarding the physical feasibility of achieving <0.03 reflectance with these materials and constraints. Stopping now would be premature as we have not yet tested either of the two physically distinct hypotheses. We must proceed to test at least one configuration to determine if the physics allows for low reflectance, and potentially the other if the first fails or shows promise.\",\n  \"insight_for_next\": \"Split the current ambiguous request into two separate, concrete experiments. Experiment A: Fix the stack order as Air / SiO2 (bottom) / TiO2 (top) / Glass. Experiment B: Fix the stack order as Air / TiO2 (bottom) / SiO2 (top) / Glass. Run Experiment A first with the specified bounds (40-160 nm) and seed 17. If Experiment A yields a valid best score, evaluate Experiment B in a subsequent round to compare order